From c616201608bb7b20a021a551e4b92f5a1b5464f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:40:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: Add deblocking filter controls for HFI gen2

Iris does not expose deblocking filter controls for HFI gen2 encoder
sessions, leaving applications unable to configure the filter mode or its
offsets.

Expose the standard V4L2 H.264 loop filter mode, alpha and beta controls
and the HEVC loop filter mode, tc and beta controls. Register them in both
gen2 encoder capability tables with filtering enabled and zero offsets by
default. Allow changes before streaming starts.

Translate the codec-specific mode enums and pack the offsets, biased by
six, into HFI_PROP_DEBLOCKING_MODE. Only send the controls for the active
codec so that the other codec's settings cannot overwrite them.

Signed-off-by: Xilin Wu <sophon@radxa.com>
